{
  "dom_id": "step-q127807",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Which of the following vector-valued functions are continuous on $[-1,1]?$\n\n  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(s) & =|{s}^{2}-1|\\,i+\\frac{s+1}{s}\\,j+2{s}^{2}\\,k \\\\ q(s) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s-1)\\,i+({s}^{2}+1)\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡s\\,k \\\\ r(s) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡s\\,i-2\\operatorname{tan}⁡s\\,j+\\operatorname{csc}⁡s\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "A vector-valued function is continuous on an interval if and only if each of its components is continuous on that interval.  \n\nLet's consider the functions one by one. \n\n- The function $p(s)$ is **not** continuous on $[-1,1]$ because \nits second component, $\\frac{s+1}{s},$ is undefined at $s=0$ and hence discontinuous on $[-1,1].$\n\n- The function $q(s)$ is **not** continuous on $[-1,1]$ because \nits first component, $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s-1)$, is undefined at $s=1$ and hence discontinuous on $[-1,1].$\n\n- The function $r(s)$ is **not** continuous on $[-1,1]$ because \nits third component, $\\operatorname{csc}⁡s$, is undefined at $s=0$ and hence discontinuous on $[-1,1].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the functions are continuous on $[-1,1].$\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
